 "stem": "If $C({=m1}, {=m2})$ is the midpoint of $\\overline{AB}$ where $A({=a1}, {=a2})$, find the coordinates of the point $B$. Write your answer as $(x, y)$.",
 "solution": [
  "Let $B(x_2, y_2)$. Then $A({=a1}, {=a2})$ and the midpoint is $C({=m1}, {=m2})$.",
  "Use $x=\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2}$: ${=m1}=\\frac{({=a1})+x_2}{2}$, so $({=a1})+x_2={=2*m1}$, hence $x_2={=b1}$.",
